  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="02aa-a6d9-01fc-63ee" name="Pergamene (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #32 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The kingdom of Pergamon in North West Asia Minor gained its independence upon the collapse of Lysimachus’ short-lived state. Under the Attalid dynasty it became an ally of Rome and thus found itself on the winning side against the Macedonians and Seleucids, and expanded at Seleucid expense. Its last king cannily bequeathed the kingdom to Rome, and it thus became a province without the usual inconvenience of being conquered. Allies: The army may have allied contingents from the Twilight of Greece and Galatian lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Pergamene]
  Cavalry: up to 40%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  War Machines, Allies and Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 40% Infantry: At least 25% War Machines, Allies and Mercenaries: Up to 50% Elephants: 0-1 per 1,200 points, taken from the Seleucid list.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
